---
import GrantPlayground from '../../components/demo/GrantPlayground.astro';
import Demo from '../../layouts/Demo.astro';
---

<Demo
	title="Grant playground"
	description="An agent acting for someone gets the overlap of three things: what the person can do, what the agent may ever do, and what the task needs. Try it."
>
	<GrantPlayground slot="demo" />

	<h2>What you're looking at</h2>
	<p>
		Every row is a tool call the agent could make. It's allowed only if all three checks say
		yes. Hover a ✓ or ✗ to see why.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Person:</strong> could Ana or Ben do this themselves? An agent never gets more than
			the person it works for.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Agent:</strong> the most this agent may ever do, set by its owner. report-bot may
			never touch export-controlled data, whoever it works for.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Task:</strong> what this job needs. A headcount review covers HR, but not tools
			tagged <code>pii</code> unless the task names pii, and pii fields come back masked.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Press <strong>Call</strong> and the decision is written to the ledger before the answer goes
		out. Each entry carries a hash of the one before it, so rewriting history breaks the chain.
		Press <strong>Tamper</strong>, then <strong>Verify</strong>.
	</p>

	<h2>Things to try</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Headcount review, then the same task "with pii": watch payroll's <code>salary</code> unmask and performance reviews open up.</li>
		<li>Switch the agent to support-bot on the Q3 close: its ceiling doesn't include finance.</li>
		<li>Act for Ben on the Q3 close: the person check fails on HR and market data.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>The real thing</h2>
	<p>
		This page is a small JavaScript copy of the rules, so it runs in your browser. The real
		engine is <a href="https://github.com/FatherBrian/trellis">Trellis</a>: it compiles each check
		to its own <a href="https://www.cedarpolicy.com/">Cedar</a> policy set, signs grants and
		ledger checkpoints, and can sit behind an MCP gateway like Reef. Try it with
		<code>pip install trellisd</code> and <code>trellisd demo three-keys</code>.
	</p>
</Demo>
